  "solution": {
    "text": "In ccp,  <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  ions are 4.<br >        Hence total negative charge = -8<br >        Let  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  ions be x, and  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  ions be y.<br >        Total positive charge = 3x + 2y<br >         <math><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> <br >        This relation is satisfied only by x = 2 and y = 1.<br >        Hence number of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> <br >        and number of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> <br >         <math><mo>⇒</mo></math>  n = fraction of octahedral holes occupied by  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> <br >         <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> <br >        and m = fraction of tetrahedral holes occupied by  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> <br >         <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  }
}